  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): Duplicate of INV-nugos-domil-sutag-johol-lifol-pijuv-faruh-zibuj. Same mechanism (slice.py:153 ambiguity-error template appends --language suggestion unconditionally), same fix-direction (branch on len({c.language for c in candidates})). INV-nugos is the later-filed but more detailed write-up (reproduces with cli:main matching two same-language files); WI-kutam reproduces with find_files (real symbol vs python:external:0-0:<name>:unresolved synthetic — same language). Co-fix with INV-nogof under a shared ambiguity-resolution helper."  # cecc
- op: discuss  # 5402
  at: '2026-05-30T21:08:14Z'  # 5402
  by: agent  # 5402
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5402
  clock: 4  # 5402
  nonce: '5402'  # 5402
  message: "Fold-in from INV-nugos-domil (pending human delete; dogfood_anon_id ITEM-911ce4 — distinct from this item's ITEM-c4e371) ahead of duplicate removal:\n\n(1) Second repro example — same mechanism, different candidate-set shape: `hypergumbo slice --entry cli:main --input bm.json` rejects with 'Ambiguous entry cli:main matches 2 symbols in different files: [python] packages/hypergumbo-tracker/.../cli.py, [python] packages/hypergumbo-core/.../cli.py. Use a full node ID to disambiguate, or filter with --language.' Re-running with `--language python` produces the same error (both candidates share that language). This is the same slice.py:153 template defect as this item's find_files repro, demonstrated on a same-language same-name cross-package collision instead of a real-vs-synthetic collision.\n\n(2) Alternative fix angle — INV-nugos proposed: when the shared-language case is detected, suggest `--file` / `--path` instead, or have the error emit `module:name` with the package qualifier so users can copy a disambiguated form directly. Complementary to this item's --list-entries / copy-full-ID suggestion.\n\n(3) Invariant phrasing from INV-nugos (for the eventual fix-side property test): 'When slice rejects an ambiguous entry, its error message should not suggest --language as a remedy if the ambiguous candidates already share a language; the suggested fix should be applicable.' Root cause: 'Slice ambiguity error template unconditionally appends or filter with --language, without checking whether the language axis actually splits the candidate set.'\n\n(4) Co-fix scope: INV-nogof (related ambiguity-resolution item, mentioned in this thread on 2026-05-30) remains a co-fix candidate under a shared ambiguity-resolution helper.\n\nAfter this fold-in lands, INV-nugos is safe for human delete (duplicate_of marker already set)."  # 5402
